* Pestifer-supplied CHARMM parameters: resolutions where the release conflicts with itself
*
* The shipped CHARMM release defines a small number of terms MORE THAN ONCE, in different
* files, with different values. CHARMM resolves this by load order -- "In all cases the
* final version of a parameter is the one used for the calculations" (toppar_all.history,
* entry 2026_1_24) -- so which value a build gets depends on which file was read last
* rather than on any judgment about which value is right.
*
* This file records the cases where that judgment HAS been made, and asserts the chosen
* value explicitly. It is loaded last (schema: charmmff.custom.prm), so an entry here wins
* regardless of the order the conflicting sources happened to be read in. Choosing here
* rather than by reordering the release's own files keeps the decision visible, auditable,
* and confined to the one term it is about.
*
* IMPORTANT: this file is for terms the release defines TWICE. It is not a place to
* override a parameter pestifer merely disagrees with, and it is not a fill for missing
* parameters -- degenerate-torsion fills live in toppar_pestifer_dihedral_fills.prm, and a
* genuinely absent parameter must remain an error. Every entry names both conflicting
* sources, both values, and why one was chosen.
*
* Provenance: pestifer (Cameron F. Abrams). Not part of any upstream CHARMM release.
*

DIHEDRALS
! atom-i  atom-j  atom-k  atom-l    Kchi   n   delta
!
! NG2O1-CG2R61-CG2R61-NG2S3 (nitro and primary amine para/meta on one aromatic ring).
! Defined twice in the release, a factor of 2.48 apart:
!   par_all36_cgenff.prm         1.2500  2  180.00  ! aa, 23007G
!   toppar_all36_carb_imlab.str  3.1000  2  180.00  ! "from, NG2S3 CG2R61 CG2R61 NG2S3"
! The imlab value is derived BY ANALOGY from the DIAMINE quartet (two amines) and was
! appended under a "!DNAP" label for one ligand in a glycan-patch stream; CHARMM's append
! has no scoping, so it silently applied to every molecule in the system. The CGenFF value
! is a fitted CGenFF parameter. Provenance also favors it: par_all36_cgenff.prm was revised
! 2026_1_24 with "the bonded parameters aligned" and released as v5.0 on 2026_2_14, while
! toppar_all36_carb_imlab.str is absent from the 2026 change log entirely and its last
! recorded change is 2021_11_1. Chosen by Cameron F. Abrams, 2026-09-28.
NG2O1  CG2R61 CG2R61 NG2S3     1.2500   2   180.00 ! CGenFF v5.0 value, chosen over imlab's analogy value

END
